From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:07:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] fix: keep access chain flag on copied pointers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: Metal compile errors and failed compute PSOs in PRAGMATA; stores
through a copied pointer emitted "*arr[i] = x".

Root cause: OpCopyObject of a pointer to an access chain produced an
expression without the access_chain flag, so it was treated as a raw
pointer and dereferenced. dxil-spirv emits this pattern for groupshared
stores.

Fix: inherit access_chain and need_transpose from the source expression
when copying a pointer.

Verified by: 0 Metal compile failures in PRAGMATA after the fix, about
twice as many shaders reach compilation (see NOTES.md §16).

Off switch: none.
---
 spirv_glsl.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/spirv_glsl.cpp b/spirv_glsl.cpp
index c8284a2..79db239 100644
--- a/spirv_glsl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_glsl.cpp
@@ -13988,6 +13988,13 @@ void CompilerGLSL::emit_instruction(const Instruction &instruction)
 			{
 				e.implied_read_expressions = rhs_expr->implied_read_expressions;
 				e.expression_dependencies = rhs_expr->expression_dependencies;
+				// A copied pointer to an access chain is still an access chain (an lvalue), not a raw
+				// pointer; without this, stores through the copy get a bogus dereference ("*arr[i] = x").
+				if (pointer)
+				{
+					e.access_chain = rhs_expr->access_chain;
+					e.need_transpose = rhs_expr->need_transpose;
+				}
 			}
 		}
 		break;
